<title>INDIA: India M3 money supply rises to 16.4 pct on May 23.</title>
<headline>India M3 money supply rises to 16.4 pct on May 23.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-06-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's year-on-year M3 money supply growth was 16.4 percent on May 23, compared to 16.3 percent on May 9, the Reserve Bank of India (RBI) said in its weekly statistical supplement on Monday.  </p>
<p>		   M3 MONEY SUPPLY GROWTH (yr-on-yr in pct)</p>
<p>		   May 23, 1997   May 9, 1997   May 24, 1996</p>
<p>		   16.4	     16.3	    15.7</p>
<p>Money supply was 7,199.80 billion rupees on May 23 against 7,181.39 billion rupees on May 9, 1997 and 6,183.29 billion on May 24, 1996, the RBI said.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
